Lets create a new worksheet

# Worksheet Set Creation Request, Mobile first design approach, No horizontal margins/padding and no horizontal 
scrolling should be there

Wait for the following information
1. Grade level (e.g., grade2, preschool)
2. Subject (e.g., mathematics, art)
3. Topic (e.g., multiplication, color_mixing)
4. Difficulty level (beginner, intermediate, advanced)
5. Learning objectives and key features

# Development Steps

1. Create folder structure:
   [grade]_[subject]_[topic]_[difficulty]/

2. File Structure:
   [grade]_[subject]_[topic]_[difficulty]/
   ├── components/
   │   ├── [Prefix]Worksheet.tsx
   │   ├── [Prefix]AnswerKey.tsx
   │   ├── [Prefix]Tips.tsx
   │   └── [Prefix]Thumbnail.tsx
   ├── entries/
   │   └── index.tsx
   ├── title.txt
   └── description.txt

2. Create and implement components in this order:
   a. Main Worksheet ([Prefix]Worksheet.tsx)
      - Mobile first design approach, No horizontal margins/padding on root containers
      - Core interactive learning content
      - Student input and feedback mechanisms
      - Score tracking
      - Visual aids and examples
      

   **Important**: After creating the worksheet component, verify and proceed after confirmation:
      - All interactive features work as expected
      - Score tracking is accurate
      - Feedback mechanisms are clear
      - Visual aids are appropriate
      - Content matches learning objectives
   Only proceed to other components after confirming worksheet functionality.

   b. Answer Key ([Prefix]AnswerKey.tsx)
      - Mobile first design approach, No horizontal margins/padding on root containers
      - Solutions with explanations
      - Step-by-step guidance
      - Visual demonstrations

   c. Tips ([Prefix]Tips.tsx)
      - Mobile first design approach, No horizontal margins/padding on root containers
      - Specific strategies for this worksheet
      - Problem-solving guidance
      - Quick reference aids

   d. Title and Description
      - title.txt (max 6 words, clear and descriptive)
      - description.txt (clear summary of content and objectives)

   e. Thumbnail ([Prefix]Thumbnail.tsx)
      - Outer container: 500x375px (4:3 ratio)
      - Inner container: 420x240px (centered)
      - Background: gradient from pink to yellow
      - Inner content: white container with shadow
      - System font stack

3. Create entry point (entries/index.tsx):
   ```typescript
   import '../../../index.css';
   import { lazy, Suspense } from 'react';
   import { createRoot } from 'react-dom/client';

   // Lazy load components
   const Worksheet = lazy(() => import('../components/[Prefix]Worksheet'));
   const AnswerKey = lazy(() => import('../components/[Prefix]AnswerKey'));
   const Tips = lazy(() => import('../components/[Prefix]Tips'));
   const Thumbnail = lazy(() => import('../components/[Prefix]Thumbnail'));

   // Required type declaration for worksheet view
   declare global {
     interface Window {
       WORKSHEET_VIEW: 'worksheet' | 'answer_key' | 'tips' | 'thumbnail';
       WORKSHEET_METADATA: {
         id: string;
         title: string;
         description: string;
         metadata: {
           grade: string;
           subject: string;
           topic: string;
           difficulty: string;
         };
       };
     }
   }

   const view = window.WORKSHEET_VIEW || 'worksheet';

   const App = () => {
     const getComponent = () => {
       switch (view) {
         case 'worksheet': return <Worksheet />;
         case 'answer_key': return <AnswerKey />;
         case 'tips': return <Tips />;
         case 'thumbnail': return <Thumbnail />;
         default: return <Worksheet />;
       }
     };

     return (
       <Suspense fallback={<div>Loading...</div>}>
         {getComponent()}
       </Suspense>
     );
   };

   // Initialize React
   const rootElement = document.getElementById('root');
   if (rootElement) {
     const root = createRoot(rootElement);
     root.render(<App />);
   }
   ```
   - React initialization and view switching
   - Component lazy loading
   - Global type declarations for WORKSHEET_VIEW and WORKSHEET_METADATA
   - Proper error boundaries with Suspense
   - Default view fallback to worksheet
   - No manual HTML file creation needed (auto-generated during build)



4. Build and Verify:
   ```powershell
   $env:WORKSHEET_ID="[grade]_[subject]_[topic]_[difficulty]"; npm run build
   ```
   - Verify all HTML files load correctly
   - Check all interactive features
   - Test responsive design
   - Validate thumbnail generation

# Technical Requirements

- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Implement lazy loading
- Follow TypeScript best practices
- Ensure mobile responsiveness
- Include proper error handling
- Add loading states
- Implement proper accessibility
